# Structured citation metadata (Citation File Format 1.2.0).
# GitHub renders this as the repository's "Cite this repository" button.
#
# NOTE: `doi` below is the Zenodo *concept* DOI, which always resolves to the latest version.
# After the v4.0.0 Zenodo deposit is published, add the version-specific DOI as an
# `identifiers:` entry.
# The software author is Ben Kennedy; "Levy Tate" is an alias under which the accompanying
# book chapter cites this software ("Tate, L."), preserved here so those citations resolve.
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using these metadata."
title: "STAC: Spiking Transformer Augmenting Cognition"
abstract: >-
  A research framework and study of converting pretrained transformer language models
  (DistilGPT-2, SmolLM2) into spiking neural networks. Includes a measured account of
  conversion fidelity, an operation-count energy analysis, evidence that post-hoc conversion
  of a frozen model collapses without training, and a spike-aware fine-tuning path.
type: software
